WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.786 --> 00:00:03.998
how excited I was to meet you.

00:00:03.998 --> 00:00:06.008
We're all so thrilled you're here.

00:00:06.008 --> 00:00:07.099
- Oh, I'm thrilled to be there.

00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:09.175
Hi, everybody. Hey.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.168
What a great audience.

00:00:11.168 --> 00:00:12.135
- [Drew] Thank you.

00:00:12.135 --> 00:00:12.968
- Wow. My pleasure.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:16.358
- So wait, okay, you
did the wacky wire game.

00:00:16.358 --> 00:00:17.927
First of all, what is that?

00:00:17.927 --> 00:00:19.370
- I don't even know.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.641
(audience laughs)
(Drew laughs)

00:00:22.641 --> 00:00:24.488
I was a law student at the time,

00:00:24.488 --> 00:00:27.248
but we took a summer out and
it was a work exchange program

00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:29.018
and all my buddies went
to work in the carnival.

00:00:29.018 --> 00:00:31.028
And the next minute I'm
standing behind this wacky wire,

00:00:31.028 --> 00:00:33.188
which is a wire that goes down like this

00:00:33.188 --> 00:00:36.038
with a board behind and,
you have to take a loop,

00:00:36.038 --> 00:00:38.490
metal loop, and take it round that loop

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.298
without touching the wire.

00:00:40.298 --> 00:00:41.498
And if you touch it, it's over.

00:00:41.498 --> 00:00:44.198
And if you don't touch it,

00:00:44.198 --> 00:00:46.378
you win the biggest
teddy bear in the fair!

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:49.208
(audience cheers)

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:51.695
- It's sort of like Operation.

00:00:51.695 --> 00:00:52.724
You know that game?
- Yes!

00:00:52.724 --> 00:00:53.557
- Where like

00:00:53.557 --> 00:00:54.425
if you touch the metal.
- That's exactly.

00:00:54.425 --> 00:00:56.783
And the first person that came up to play

00:00:56.783 --> 00:01:00.458
was a little kid and he just
walked up and he gave me $2.

00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:02.498
And I'm like, I can't do this.

00:01:02.498 --> 00:01:03.908
I just can't take people's money.

00:01:03.908 --> 00:01:05.888
This is awful. I felt so bad.

00:01:05.888 --> 00:01:08.168
Few days later I'm like,
"Hey kiddo, gimme that money.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.818
Come on, gimme your money.

00:01:09.818 --> 00:01:11.615
Biggest teddy bear in the fair."

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:15.278
- Well, okay, so how...

00:01:15.278 --> 00:01:16.598
I didn't know this about you.

00:01:16.598 --> 00:01:19.058
You were a fully fledged lawyer.

00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:20.558
Like, a real lawyer.

00:01:20.558 --> 00:01:22.159
- Like a lawyer.

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:24.188
Yeah, I was like a
lawyer, not just a lawyer.

00:01:24.188 --> 00:01:26.013
- No, but that's actually not true.

00:01:26.013 --> 00:01:27.118
- Oh, it's not.

00:01:27.118 --> 00:01:28.328
- Well, it's mostly true.

00:01:28.328 --> 00:01:31.808
I went through law school,
I got a honors law degree,

00:01:31.808 --> 00:01:33.308
I got a diploma in legal practice.

00:01:33.308 --> 00:01:36.668
I did my two years training
to become a lawyer.

00:01:36.668 --> 00:01:37.501
- [Drew] And?

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:40.958
- Minus a week, and I
wasn't doing very well.

00:01:40.958 --> 00:01:42.128
I hated what I was doing.

00:01:42.128 --> 00:01:43.118
I wanna be an actor.

00:01:43.118 --> 00:01:45.721
And about a week before
they sat me down, they said,

00:01:45.721 --> 00:01:48.038
"This isn't really for you, is it?

00:01:48.038 --> 00:01:49.508
This is not really what you wanna do?"

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:52.538
Kept going, and I became
the first trainee lawyer

00:01:52.538 --> 00:01:56.348
in the history of the Scottish
legal system to be fired.

00:01:56.348 --> 00:01:57.566
So I'm kinda proud of that.

00:01:57.566 --> 00:02:00.788
But the next day I packed
my bags, moved to London,

00:02:00.788 --> 00:02:01.746
and that was it.

00:02:01.746 --> 00:02:03.991
I said this is in a way I've been released

00:02:03.991 --> 00:02:05.498
to do what I wanna do.

00:02:05.498 --> 00:02:07.921
- Okay, so I was looking at your IMDB,

00:02:07.921 --> 00:02:11.945
but it was like a while before "300."

00:02:11.945 --> 00:02:14.648
You know, you had been in
the business for a while,

00:02:14.648 --> 00:02:18.887
but then when that movie hits,
oh my God, it hits so hard.

00:02:18.887 --> 00:02:21.887
(audience cheering)

00:02:25.462 --> 00:02:28.088
This Is such a major movie.

00:02:28.088 --> 00:02:29.978
It's not only a box office success,

00:02:29.978 --> 00:02:32.168
it's like a cult classic at the same time.

00:02:32.168 --> 00:02:33.968
It's like, it's everything.

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.458
- Yeah, 'cause it fires
you up to, you know,

00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:37.628
what are we gonna do?

00:02:37.628 --> 00:02:39.525
- I don't know, but I love it!
- Yeah!

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:42.488
- And is it true that like, this is Sparta

00:02:42.488 --> 00:02:45.098
was a line in the script,
but it's really you

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.048
that like gave it that energy and life?

00:02:47.048 --> 00:02:48.368
What possessed?

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.988
- Well, yeah, because I was, you know,

00:02:49.988 --> 00:02:51.908
we'd have that conversation
and go, you know,

00:02:51.908 --> 00:02:54.878
this is madness, and I was, "Madness?"

00:02:54.878 --> 00:02:56.948
This is Sparta." Boom.

00:02:56.948 --> 00:02:59.312
I did a few takes like that, one a little.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.248
(audience cheers)

00:03:00.248 --> 00:03:04.808
I did one a little louder,
and then the scene was done

00:03:04.808 --> 00:03:05.641
and they were moving on.

00:03:05.641 --> 00:03:07.088
The guys are canning the camera away.

00:03:07.088 --> 00:03:07.921
- [Drew] Oh God!

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:08.754
- I go, no, no, no, no, no!

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:10.148
Wait, wait, wait, wait
'cause I suddenly thought,

00:03:10.148 --> 00:03:11.768
what about the wildness in these men?

00:03:11.768 --> 00:03:13.568
There's a wildness and a surprise

00:03:13.568 --> 00:03:15.548
and it's like, I can
have that conversation

00:03:15.548 --> 00:03:17.948
and then you go, oh, this
is who they really are.

00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:19.328
So they bring it back.

00:03:19.328 --> 00:03:20.708
I went, "Madness?

00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:23.588
This is Sparta!" Boom!

00:03:23.588 --> 00:03:25.418
And they went cut, and I turn around

00:03:25.418 --> 00:03:26.978
and everybody was laughing behind me

00:03:26.978 --> 00:03:28.838
because it just seems so.

00:03:28.838 --> 00:03:30.518
And I go over to the
director and I'm like,

00:03:30.518 --> 00:03:31.358
that was too much, right?

00:03:31.358 --> 00:03:32.318
He goes, "Yeah!

00:03:32.318 --> 00:03:33.681
But it was awesome!

00:03:33.681 --> 00:03:36.681
(audience applauds)

00:03:37.688 --> 00:03:39.368
- Okay, you're in this new action thriller

00:03:39.368 --> 00:03:40.948
that I'm obsessed with, "Plane."

00:03:40.948 --> 00:03:42.188
We have a clip.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.088
Let's take a look.

00:03:44.708 --> 00:03:48.458
- There is no full rescue
team coming anytime, sir.

00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:50.377
Not for the next 24 hours.

00:03:50.377 --> 00:03:52.298
All right, we can't wait.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.527
They're gonna come at us
with everything they've got,

00:03:54.527 --> 00:03:56.593
and we're not gonna survive.

00:03:56.593 --> 00:03:59.648
Now Danny and I managed to get the power

00:03:59.648 --> 00:04:01.457
back up on the plane.

00:04:01.457 --> 00:04:05.468
I know we have one chance, and that is me

00:04:05.468 --> 00:04:06.972
flying us outta here on this thing.

00:04:06.972 --> 00:04:08.257
- Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:04:08.257 --> 00:04:09.743
(audience cheering)

00:04:09.743 --> 00:04:11.031
- I didn't even see that clip.

00:04:11.031 --> 00:04:12.368
- I luckily watched the clip.

00:04:12.368 --> 00:04:13.208
I've seen the film.

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:17.629
Okay, so this film is
so juicy I have to say.

00:04:17.629 --> 00:04:19.028
- Juicy is a good word.
- It really is.

00:04:19.028 --> 00:04:21.188
It's like, it just, It gives you

00:04:21.188 --> 00:04:23.484
all of that yummy stuff you crave

00:04:23.484 --> 00:04:26.553
when you go to an action film.

00:04:26.553 --> 00:04:28.658
Did you do pilot training for this?

00:04:28.658 --> 00:04:29.738
- I did do pilot training.

00:04:29.738 --> 00:04:32.318
I spent a lot of time in a simulator.

00:04:32.318 --> 00:04:34.628
I had two of the coolest
pilots with me all the time.

00:04:34.628 --> 00:04:35.461
- Really?

00:04:35.461 --> 00:04:36.807
- Yeah, they trained me in the simulator.

00:04:36.807 --> 00:04:40.178
So in the simulator, you
really feel like you're flying

00:04:40.178 --> 00:04:43.028
and what you're looking
at digitally is so real.

00:04:43.028 --> 00:04:46.778
You're watching cars, and the
405, I passed my old house,

00:04:46.778 --> 00:04:48.488
I went under the Hollywood sign,

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:50.119
I'm taking a photos as I'm
flying the plane going,

00:04:50.119 --> 00:04:52.058
look, this is me at the Hollywood sign

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:55.358
because a lot of the movie,
you're flying a, you know,

00:04:55.358 --> 00:04:58.388
basically it's like a 737 over the ocean,

00:04:58.388 --> 00:05:01.358
onto the island looking for a
place to land in the jungle,

00:05:01.358 --> 00:05:03.026
and the river back out in the ocean back.

00:05:03.026 --> 00:05:05.318
So that's what I was doing in LA.

00:05:05.318 --> 00:05:06.901
I was flying over the 405, the 101

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.272
because if you're playing the pilot

00:05:08.272 --> 00:05:10.778
you wanna immerse the
audience in this world.

00:05:10.778 --> 00:05:12.638
And I feel like those
scenes, you really feel like

00:05:12.638 --> 00:05:14.918
you're in that cockpit with
us going through the storm,

00:05:14.918 --> 00:05:16.478
having to make the decisions that we make

00:05:16.478 --> 00:05:18.098
because this guy is a hero, but he's not.

00:05:18.098 --> 00:05:19.058
He's a regular guy.

00:05:19.058 --> 00:05:21.578
It's like, what do these
situations pull outta you

00:05:21.578 --> 00:05:23.877
when an ordinary person
suddenly finds himself

00:05:23.877 --> 00:05:25.928
in these extraordinary situations?

00:05:25.928 --> 00:05:27.938
And I love making those movies

00:05:27.938 --> 00:05:29.018
where they're flesh and blood.

00:05:29.018 --> 00:05:29.888
They make mistakes.

00:05:29.888 --> 00:05:32.042
You know, he doesn't get it
right this guy, but he tries.

00:05:32.042 --> 00:05:34.122
(audience cheering)

00:05:34.122 --> 00:05:37.289
(upbeat bright music)

